From 1e0a752e19d319ea863f8fd453a41fae927935ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:08:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] camera_edge: forward frames to camera-processor
 (CAMERA_PROCESSING=remote)

Moves the image processing off the camera Pi. With CAMERA_PROCESSING=remote,
camera_edge keeps talking to camera_host, waiting for the PLC and numbering
each run's frames, but no longer decodes frames or runs ArUco detection +
PnP. Each JPEG from camera_host is published unchanged on
camera_frames/<DEVICE_ID>_<CAMERA_NAME>/frame, with a retained .../config
message carrying the calibration and detection settings. camera-processor
(wku-smr-lab-middleware, camera_processor/) runs the same detection and
publishes the same rows on camera/<DEVICE_ID>_<CAMERA_NAME>.

CAMERA_PROCESSING defaults to local, so existing deployments are unchanged.

- camera_edge/frame_forwarder.py: wire format + MQTT publisher (bounded
  queue, drops and counts frames while the broker is down)
- config: CAMERA_PROCESSING, CAMERA_FRAME_BROKER_IP/_PORT,
  CAMERA_FRAME_TOPIC_PREFIX, CAMERA_FRAME_QOS
- agent: remote mode skips local session folders and outputs; one run_id
  per PLC run so camera-processor opens a run folder per run
- tests/test_camera_edge_remote.py, scripts/remote_processing_smoke.py
  (end-to-end; checks remote rows == local rows for the same JPEG)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BMfRtKBVPGk558yGXkuWf3
